    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0529" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg441"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Grubb.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Newberry’s dispatch No.
                    205, of the 26th ultimo, containing a résumé of his correspondence with the
                    Spanish Government, concerning the late disturbances at Ponape, Caroline
                    Islands, recently the subject of instructions to Mr. Newberry. Awaiting the
                    receipt of the reply of the Duke of Tetuan,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
